cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below. Please also cite the data and tools it depends on; see the README's 'Data credits and licences' section."
type: software
title: "planet-hunter: an open search of TESS light curves for planet candidates"
abstract: >-
  planet-hunter searches public NASA TESS light curves for repeating transit-like dips.
  It vets each signal with flux-level checks, catalogue cross-matching, a difference-image
  pixel check and published community tools, and it measures its own sensitivity by
  injection-recovery. Its outputs are planet candidates, never confirmed planets.
authors:
  - family-names: Anastasiadis
    given-names: Foivos
repository-code: "https://github.com/anastasiadisfoivos-hub/planet-hunter"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - exoplanets
  - TESS
  - transit search
  - planet candidates
  - vetting
  - astronomy
